{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_96","type":"agent_message","text":"Created [solution_12.py](/root/solution_12.py) with a TensorCircuit-NG JAX-backed implementation.\n\nThe solution:\n- Converts the provided quimb MPS into TensorCircuit-NG's MPS representation.\n- Builds the two-layer brickwork SU(4) circuit from the Néel state using `tc.MPSCircuit`.\n- Runs exactly 5000 Adam updates via `jax.lax.scan`, recording loss and fidelity before each update.\n- Returns the 5000-step histories, final parameters, and final overlap phase.\n\nIn a local end-to-end test with the same configuration and a quimb DMRG target, it completed in about 15 seconds, with final fidelity ≈ 0.870, final loss ≈ 0.130, and all arrays finite and correctly shaped."}}
